---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const contactEmail = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_CONTACT_EMAIL || 'hello@poteto.fun';
---

<Layout
  title="About Poteto — The Daily Human Qualification Audit"
  description="How Poteto works: zero-login daily global CAPTCHA seeds, 500-byte vector potato doodles, and three-layer anti-spam safety."
  canonicalPath="/about"
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6">
    <div class="rounded-3xl border border-[#E4E4E7] bg-white p-6 shadow-xs sm:p-10">
      <span class="font-mono text-xs font-bold tracking-wider text-[#1A73E8] uppercase">
        ABOUT POTETO
      </span>
      <h1 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-[#09090B] sm:text-3xl">
        Why are we competing against an Idaho potato to stay human?
      </h1>

      <div class="mt-6 space-y-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[#3F3F46]">
        <p>
          Every day we click &ldquo;I&apos;m not a robot&rdquo; and hunt for grainy crosswalks just to prove our humanity to algorithms.
          <strong>Poteto</strong> flips that ritual into a 90-second daily comedy audit: instead of outsmarting AI, you go head-to-head against a completely unbothered Idaho russet (Spud #01).
        </p>

        <h2 class="pt-2 font-display text-lg font-bold text-[#09090B]">Core Design Principles</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li><strong>Zero Login Friction</strong>: No sign-ups, no popups. Your streak and yesterday&apos;s doodle stats stay tied to an anonymous local UUID.</li>
          <li><strong>Global Deterministic Seed</strong>: Seeded daily by UTC date so every player worldwide gets the exact same 3-stage audit.</li>
          <li><strong>Ultra-Light Vector UGC</strong>: Hand-drawn potatoes are normalized to a 0–100 grid and simplified via Ramer-Douglas-Peucker to 300–600 bytes of JSON—zero image uploads.</li>
          <li><strong>Three-Layer Safety Net</strong>: 4-stroke / 10-second / closed-loop constraints upfront, next-day curated pool isolation, and automatic 3-flag community takedowns.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="pt-2 font-display text-lg font-bold text-[#09090B]">Say Hello</h2>
        <p>
          Got an even more unhinged Stage 2 mini-game idea or feedback? Drop us a line at{' '}
          <a
            href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}
            class="font-mono font-semibold text-[#1A73E8] underline underline-offset-2"
          >
            {contactEmail}
          </a>
          .
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
